    "q-162633": {
      "dom_id": "step-q162633",
      "name": "Question 4",
      "problem": "The domain of the vector-valued function $f(t)=(1-\\operatorname{cot}⁡t)\\,i+\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t\\,j+{t}^{2}\\,k$ is \n\n$$\nt\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ),\\,t\\ne \\bbox[5pt,border:1pt solid black]{\\phantom{AAAAA}}.\n$$\n\nWhat is the missing expression? You may assume that $n$ is an integer.",
      "worked_solution": "To find the domain of $f$, we need the intersection of the domains of the individual components.\n\n- The domain of the 1st component $1-\\operatorname{cot}⁡t$ is $t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ),$ , $t\\ne n\\pi ,$ where $n$ is an integer.\n\n- The domain of the 2nd component $\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t$ is $t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).$\n\n- The domain of the 3rd component ${t}^{2}$ is $t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).$\n\nTherefore, the domain of the vector-valued function $f(t)$ is \n\n$$\nt\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ),\\,t\\ne n\\pi ,\n$$\n\nwhere $n$ is an integer.",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
          "choices": [
            {
              "option": "a",
              "dom_id": "questionWidget-choiceLetterCircle-162633-a",
