    "q-162652": {
      "dom_id": "step-q162652",
      "name": "Question 5",
      "problem": "Find the domain of the vector-valued function $f(s)=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(s-2)\\,i+(1-s)\\,j+{s}^{2}\\,k.$",
      "worked_solution": "To find the domain of $f$, we need the intersection of the domains of the individual components.\n\n- The domain of the 1st component $\\operatorname{ln}⁡(s-2)$ is $s\\in (2,\\infty ).$\n\n- The domain of the 2nd component $1-s$ is $s\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).$\n\n- The domain of the 3rd component ${s}^{2}$ is $s\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).$\n\nThe intersection is illustrated in the diagram below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/differential/14266735/assets/91b196d5e312c4242a493f65abad556aa7f689640b09e0c51bc9124681abb48a.png)\n\nTherefore, the domain of the vector-valued function $f(s)$ is $s\\in (2,\\infty ).$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
